 Once upon a time there was a priest named Huggybear. He was very lucky and
found a blessed wide sword named Stormbringer on level 1, later identified at
+2. Finding a potion shop on the level below, he quaffed the blessed potion so
kindly stolen for him by his dog. As everything suddenly looked cosmic he
cursed the Gods under his breath.

 Very soon his pet lay slain in error, and he was becoming very hungry.
Praying only revealed Crom to be displeased, and so a frantic search for food
became necessary - some was found on level 4, along with a blessd pair of hard
shoes. Strangely, these turned out to be +5.

 A ring of protection found close by gave him another three points of
protection, so by level 6 things were just about under control once more.
At this point, a smoky potion gave rise to the appearance of one of his
ancestor's ghosts, while a water nymph was wandering around stealing items at
will, especially as he was fainting from hunger once more.

 A passing soldier ant was fought off only with the aid of Elbereth, when a
master lich decided to join the party. Running for all he was worth, he
desperately sought the secret door which would lead him to the shop on the
level, and the stairs down. Finding a trap as he searched, he retreated as the
lich advanced.

 Following the lich was the ghost, which underwent a strange transformation as
it traversed the trap. As the lich and newly formed titan cursed away in
unison, desperate measures were sought for. The cursed scroll in his backpack
could have been teleportation - instead the prized ornamental cope turned
to dust and blew away. The spellbook of invisibility could have teleported him
away, but instead deprived him of his gold.

 Facing death like a man, he fought bravely, but perished, his magical
items lost forever, never to be found again...

 I know, for I am his spirit...

 The ghost of Huggybear
